      },
      "authorAssociation": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "I doubt this was intended to mean only GET requests. It's more of a colloquialism for query params to just call them GET params. (Especially in PHP, where query params are available in the $_GET superglobal, regardless of the HTTP verb)\r\nYou are right, though: This should be reworded to say query parameters instead of using an ambiguous colloquialism, I guess.",
